.el .ds Aq '
.TH gitaway-profile-add 1  "gitaway 0.0.0" "gitaway manual"
.SH NAME
gitaway\-profile\-add \- Create a profile. Asks for anything not given as a flag
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgitaway profile add\fR [\fB\-\-endpoint\fR] [\fB\-\-server\-public\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-address\fR] [\fB\-\-home\-ssh\fR] [\fB\-\-host\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-host\fR] [\fB\-\-default\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fINAME\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a profile. Asks for anything not given as a flag
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fI<ENDPOINT>\fR
The WireGuard server\*(Aqs public address, as host:port
.TP
\fB\-\-server\-public\-key\fR \fI<SERVER_PUBLIC_KEY>\fR
The WireGuard server\*(Aqs public key
.TP
\fB\-\-address\fR \fI<ADDRESS>\fR
This device\*(Aqs tunnel address, such as 10.0.0.2/32, if already known
.TP
\fB\-\-home\-ssh\fR \fI<HOME_SSH>\fR
The SSH server used to check you\*(Aqre home, as host:port
.TP
\fB\-\-host\-key\fR \fI<HOST_KEY>\fR
That SSH server\*(Aqs public host key (one line of `ssh\-keyscan` output, without the host name)
.TP
\fB\-\-host\fR \fI<LAN=TUNNEL>\fR
A server this profile handles, as LAN=TUNNEL (for example 192.0.2.10=10.0.0.1). Repeat for several
.TP
\fB\-\-default\fR
Make this the default profile
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fINAME\fR]
The profile\*(Aqs name: lower\-case letters, digits, `\-` and `_`
